            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Key Changes This Week: Platform Traffic Preferences at Cold Start</h2>
<p>From advertising backend data this week, several notable shifts have emerged in TikTok Shop's cold start traffic distribution logic.</p>
<p>First, <strong>organic and paid traffic synergy is gaining weight</strong>. The platform now factors natural conversion data into creative quality scoring alongside ad ROI. Products relying solely on paid sales—with weak natural conversion rates—face gradually declining reach even when paid ROAS meets targets. A utility app operations team reported their cold start campaign CPM jumped after two days, traced to below-category-average natural conversion rates.</p>
<p>Second, <strong>creative style preferences are shifting more clearly</strong>. Multiple advertiser communities note this week's distribution weighting favors "lifestyle scenario" content over "product feature introduction" by roughly 15%~20%. This is especially pronounced in US Market and shows similar trends in Southeast Asian markets. Reusing last quarter's high-performing creatives directly may result in CTR decline.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Impact: From "Finding the Hit" to "Building a Pool"</h2>
<p>These shifts directly affect the cold start window: <strong>the breakthrough window is shrinking, but the required creative pool size is growing.</strong></p>
<p>Traditional cold start logic used 3~5 creatives, scaled the winner fast. Now the platform shows lower tolerance for individual creatives—if a piece doesn't show positive conversion signals within the first 500 impressions, reach drops rapidly.</p>
<p>Without a deep enough creative pool, testing efficiency plummets. One cross-border e-commerce team launching a home goods product this week followed their standard 5-creative approach. Over three days, the best-performing creative consumed only 8% of budget; the other four were nearly无效. After urgently adding 12 lifestyle scenario variants to build a proper matrix, it took 48 hours to identify a stable performer.</p>
<p><strong>The conclusion is clear: cold start is no longer about "finding a hit"—it's about "building a pool to scale."</strong></p>
<hr />
<h2>Actionable Recommendations This Week: Three Steps to Build Your Creative Pool Fast</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Complete a 15~20 Creative Matrix Within 48 Hours</h3>
<p>These creatives don't need to be polished, but must cover three core dimensions:<br />
- <strong>Scenario</strong>: At least 3 different use contexts (office, home, outdoor)<br />
- <strong>Hook</strong>: At least 4 different opening styles (pain point questions, before/after comparisons, authentic reviews, product close-ups)<br />
- <strong>Duration</strong>: Cover 5s, 15s, and 30s lengths—TikTok Shop distributes content differently by length, so multi-length coverage improves hit probability</p>
<h3>Step 2: Shift Budget Allocation from "集中型" to "分散型""</h3>
<p>Instead of $100~150/day per creative, distribute $10~20/day across 15~20 creatives. This maximizes data points for the algorithm to filter quality quickly.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Yiyu team recommendation: Set automated rules—when a creative exceeds 1.5 ROAS with daily spend over $50, automatically increase budget by 50% and pause underperformers.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Step 3: Monitor Account Balance Closely to Avoid Mid-Cold-Start Pauses</h3>
<p>This week, some accounts experienced Campaign interruption due to insufficient balance. Platform reactivation triggers a 6~12 hour model reset period, typically reducing spending efficiency by 20%~30%. During cold start, maintain account balance at 5x daily budget and enable balance warning notifications.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Weekly Takeaway</h2>
<p>TikTok Shop cold start logic is shifting from "precise hit-finding" to "pool-based screening," demanding higher upfront creative volume and scenario diversity. This week's priority: <strong>increase creative quantity, decrease per-creative budget, and let the algorithm complete screening within 48 hours.</strong> Ensure adequate account balance to avoid model reset losses from unexpected pauses.</p>
